  "answer": "The evaluation showed that the models were assessed using the Mean Opinion Score (MOS) metric, which involved a survey with native speakers to gauge performance based on different criteria [4]. A set of 200 utterances narrated by speakers were randomly selected as the testing set, which was excluded from the model training process [4]. The TTS models were used to generate voice outputs for these utterances, providing both machine-generated and human narrations for comparative analysis [4]. A Telegram bot was developed to facilitate the assessment of 30 recordings per session, focusing on qualitative criteria such as audio quality, pronunciation, naturalness, and overall comprehensibility [4]. Participants were requested to rate each criterion on a scale from 1 (bad) to 5 (excellent) [4].",
